1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Next, we need to edit the sleeve.

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
In the virtual model arm position, click on the center point.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:31,000
In this blue point, create a straight line point.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:42,000
After selecting the extension tool, click on the center point at the top, then click on the center point at the bottom to create a baseline.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Then rotate a side of the plate to make the bottom have more volume.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
After creating, click on the center point at the bottom.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:02,000
After creating, adjust the shape of the plate.

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:14,000
In the process of stretching the bottom, click on the control key to change it along the original rhythm.

9
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Then select the line at the bottom of the sleeve plate, also click on the control key to stretch along the original rhythm.

10
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Then select the line at the top of the sleeve plate, click on the control key to change it along the original rhythm.

11
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
The sleeve has been a little bit twisted here.

12
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
It's because we just fixed it to the virtual model with a sewing needle.

13
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
So the width of the sleeve is not enough.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
After stretching, simulate the clothes.

15
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
After simulation, you can see that the sleeves are much smoother.

16
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Then some adjustments, then some adjustments.

17
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Including the length of the sleeve.

18
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
And widen the sleeve a little bit.

19
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
After the modification, turn the bottom straight line point to the curve line point to make the curve line smoother.

20
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Then use the edge curve point tool to adjust the curve line at the bottom.

21
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:18,000
After simulation, reduce the particle diameter to 10 to get a better simulation effect.

22
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
After creating the sleeve plate,

23
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,000
then create the opening plate to make the embroidery effect.

24
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Use the rectangle tool to drag the 2D window to create an opening plate.

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
You can use the edge curve tool to select the width of the plate.

26
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Usually 15 to 20 centimeters is more suitable.

27
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Then use the line sewing tool to sew these plates together.

28
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:45,000
After sewing, arrange the arrangement points near the wrist.

29
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
After arranging, use the positioning ball to move it to a position that can cover the virtual model wrist.

30
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:58,000
After this simulation, you won't be able to pass your arm.

31
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:09,000
You can widen the sleeve bottom according to your needs.

32
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
After that, you have to make a belt.

33
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:16,000
The waist plate can be shortened a little bit.

34
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
It's also the same as before.

35
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Use the edge curve measurement tool to click on the waist.

36
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Since the clothing measurement board has passed the belt and the sleeve,

37
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:31,000
you need to adjust its diameter.

38
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:38,000
After adjustment, you can use the edge curve measurement tool to select the measurement board to adjust its position.

39
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:44,000
After modifying the diameter, you need to move the measurement board to apply the change.

40
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Then we have finished the measurement board removal.

41
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,000
You can remove the extra plates with the same operation as before.

42
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:04,000
If therated pins may disappear during the process, please add them.

43
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Eliminate excess plates.

44
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Remove the excess plates.

45
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
After cutting some of the plate, the felt is not close enough.

46
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Pull out some ropes to tighten the lower board

47
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Next, let's make a belt plate

48
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:32,000
First select the bottom 100 part of the front and back pieces

49
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,000
In the attribute editor, look at their 2D line length

50
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Then use the rectangle tool to click on the 2D window

51
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Width is the measurement value, height is set according to need

52
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:51,000
After creation, you can check the 3D window plate effect and adjust it

53
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Adjust the width according to need

54
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:58,000
After arranging the plate, select the line cutting tool

55
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:02,000
First click on the belt, then press the Shift key

56
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
In the same direction as the belt

57
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Click on the top line each time, then release the Shift key

58
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Then merge the sides together

59
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:21,000
After merging, change to the leather surface, the surface will be more flat

60
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:25,000
And then we will see the result

61
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:29,000
After changing, switch to the leather surface, the surface will be more flat

62
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:35,000
And then we will see the result

63
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Next, we will change the width of the belt

64
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
First click on the belt

65
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Then click on the belt

66
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Then click on the belt

